{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Observe the month of the Aviv.</b> Observe, through sustained providential attention, that Nisan be the month of the Aviv, by means of intercalation of months and years, so that they align the lunar year with the solar year." "<b>And you shall observe Pesach.</b> On the eve of the festival of Matzot." "<b>For in the month of the Aviv He brought you out.</b> He intended and desired that your exodus be at the time when the month of Aviv reaches perfection — that is, the opposition (נִגּוּד) in which the lamb, the deity of Egypt, stands opposite the sun at its full strength and the moon at its opposition." "<b>By night.</b> For that opposition occurred then at night, and since no offering is brought at night, it was necessary to advance its offering to the day before that opposition; and for this remembrance He established it so for all generations."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {2 "נִגּוּד here refers to astronomical opposition; 'the lamb, deity of Egypt' refers to Aries, venerated by Egyptians, whose zodiacal sign the sun occupied at the exodus."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:21:31.874042880Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}